      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.2 [dev]: img2img, references\n\nThe FLUX.2 [dev] workflow for img2img. Write full descriptive\nsentences and put literal text in quotes; there is no negative prompt (embedded guidance, not true CFG).\n\n**Settings**: 28 steps, guidance 2.5-4 (Distilled CFG in the Generate tab), euler, 1024×1024 (multiples of 16).\n\n## img2img\n\nThe image of **Load Image ib:img** is the starting point: **Resize to** scales it to the size of the Generate tab\n(Width / Height, its *Resize to* in img2img mode; **Use size** in the Input cell takes the size of the image),\n**VAE Encode** makes the latent, and the sampler adds noise by the **denoising** strength (0.6 here) and samples\nfrom there. The prompt describes the whole image you want. Low denoising keeps the composition and colors; high\ndenoising moves further from the image. To change one area only, use the inpaint workflow; to change the image by\nan instruction, an edit model with references.\n\nThe Generate tab is in **img2img** mode while this workflow is loaded. Send an image with **Send to the input\nimage** (B), from the editor, or upload it in the Input cell before the first queue. This workflow has no Hires.\nfix pass: upscale the result with the full workflow.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:img` | Load Image | Input cell; Send to the input image (B), the editor |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:smp` | SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed (RandomNoise), steps (Flux2Scheduler), sampling method, Distilled CFG (FluxGuidance), denoising; Resize to (Width / Height) |\n| `ib:ref:0-3` | Reference 1-4 (bypassed) | References panel |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**References** (up to 4; FLUX.2 [dev] takes up to 10, add slots by copying a column and numbering its\nloader `ib:ref:4`, ...): add images in the References panel of the Generate tab (a tab next to LoRA), by\n\"Ps sends to: reference\" from Photoshop, or by dropping them there. An empty slot is bypassed together with its\nscale and encode nodes; its **Reference Latent** stays and passes the conditioning on unchanged. Refer to the\nreferences by order in the prompt (*\"the woman from image 1 wearing the jacket from image 2\"*). Each is scaled\nto 1 MP first.\n\nPut any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here).\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt.\n\nBatch generation, model and LoRA exploration, varying parameters, PNG Info, projects and the Compare tab work\nas with every marked workflow. The ControlNet tab has no units here: ComfyUI has no ControlNet for FLUX.2 [dev];\nuse a pose or depth map as a reference instead (*\"in the pose of image 2\"*).\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux2_dev_fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/diffusion_models/flux2_dev_fp8mixed.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors)\n**vae**: [full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder/resolve/main/full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors)\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.2 [dev] (Image Bench, img2img)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
